  "prompt": "For each promotion that started from April to June 2025 (start_date from 1 April to 30 June 2025), give the average units sold per day on promotion, over the promotion's own days (its first and last day both counted), and per day in the baseline, over its 14 days. Round both to 2 decimals with ROUND. A line counts for a promotion when it carries it in order_lines.promo_id, and every such line falls within the promotion's dates; where two promotions overlap on a product, a line carries only the deeper one, so it counts once. The baseline is the 14 days just before the promotion's first day, that first day not included, and holds every sales line of the promotion's products in those days, whatever promotion the line carries. Days are sales.order_date, the UTC day of the order. A period with no sale counts 0 units. Return three columns, in this order: promo_id, promo_units_per_day and baseline_units_per_day. Return one row for each such promotion. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "promo_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "promo_units_per_day",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "baseline_units_per_day",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
